Id: ali003i
Severity: INFO
Category: services
Check: check_aliases

The indicated alias is a program alias, but the executable is not owned
by root.  This may allow the owner of the executable (or anyone gaining
access to that login ID) to gain unauthorized privileges.

It is INFO rather than a WARN because the owner expected is root and
the file named is a directory or not executable: whoever owns it can
change what it holds, but not a program that runs.

Until 3.4.0 this was reported as ali003, without the letter for its level.
